cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:3:title: "Kaggriculture compiles GEMMs with cuBLAS only"
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:4:description: "To keep the compiled-GEMM CUDA crash from recurring, every compiled Kaggriculture region runs with Inductor's max_autotune_gemm_backends set to \"ATEN\" (cuBLAS) instead of Isaiah's default \"ATEN,TRITON,CPP\", after a startup check rejects an unprobed torch, triton or NVIDIA driver. The owner asked for the outcome; the implementer chose the setting from a measured A/B (+4.5–6.5 % model-only update wall). Enforcement is CPU-tested only, and the overflow guards stay."
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:12:# Kaggriculture compiles GEMMs with cuBLAS only
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:22:The owner asked for the outcome, not for a specific mechanism. **The setting below is the implementer's measured choice.** The owner did not choose `"ATEN"` and did not review the cost.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:26:- **cuBLAS only.** Every compiled Kaggriculture region runs with `torch._inductor.config.max_autotune_gemm_backends = "ATEN"`, so compiled `mm`/`addmm`/`bmm` lower to extern cuBLAS calls. Isaiah's torch 2.9.0 default is `"ATEN,TRITON,CPP"`. Every public compile entry point applies the setting before `torch.compile`: `configure_model_compile` for the `mlp` target, and `KaggricultureTransformer.compile_transformer_trunk` itself for the `trunk` target, whether `configure_model_compile` or a caller invokes it directly. The claim lives in `python/owl/model/compile_gemm.py`.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:28:- **Probed stack only.** Before the setting, a check rejects any version the A/B did not probe. The probed versions live in one constant, `KAGGRICULTURE_PROBED_COMPILE_STACK` in `python/owl/model/compile_gemm.py`: torch 2.9.0, any local build suffix such as `+cu128`; triton 3.5.0; NVIDIA driver 595.91.07.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:29:  - GPU hosts (`torch.cuda.is_available()`) read the driver with `nvidia-smi`. A missing `nvidia-smi`, a missing triton or any unprobed driver fails.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:31:  - Hosts without CUDA, such as the owner's Mac, skip the driver check and record why; they cannot report a driver. They skip the triton check, with a recorded reason, only when triton is not installed, since Inductor emits no Triton kernels there.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:34:  - A direct `KaggricultureTransformer.compile_transformer_trunk` call runs the same stack check and claim as `configure_model_compile`. Setting `"ATEN"` by hand does not skip them.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:37:- **Telemetry.** `run_ppo` prints the claim and records it as W&B summary fields: `compile_gemm_game`, `compile_gemm_backends`, `compile_stack_torch`, `compile_stack_triton` and `compile_stack_nvidia_driver`. `MetricLogger.set_summary` now accepts strings.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:38:- **The guards stay.** `_run_trunk`'s overflow guard and chunking, and the head-extent guard, stay in place. They remain until the real-trunk backward above the bound and the production compile path are verified, as the A/B recommended.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:42:The ATEN-only GEMM A/B ran at `e1458d2` on pod `w7ia3zvxqsvs3g`. It is recorded on branch `kg/rebuild-model` at `9bdd82d` in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md` lines 259–303 and in `aten-gemm-ab-2026-09-29/`. Codex verification r1 requested edits; r2 (`verify-aten-ab-r2.md`) gave **APPROVE**.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:44:- **Correctness above the int32 bound** (lines 269–274, guard bypassed, compared element-wise with eager). Every case that failed under the default backends was correct under ATEN-only:
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:47:  - The synthetic MLP forward and backward at 4,194,305 rows were clean.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:50:  - The ATEN-only caches contain zero `triton_tem_` definitions or launches.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:60:  - `"ATEN"` is in place at every compile call, for both targets and all four modes.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:61:  - Orbit keeps `"ATEN,TRITON,CPP"` and never reads the Kaggriculture stack.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:64:  - A direct Kaggriculture trunk compile claims `"ATEN"` with the checked stack. With `"ATEN"` preset by hand and an unprobed torch, it raises before compiling and claims nothing.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:68:  - Unprobed torch (2.10.0, 2.9.1, 2.8.0), triton (3.4.0, 3.6.0) and drivers are rejected.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:69:  - A GPU host without triton or without a driver reading is rejected.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:78:  - not setting `"ATEN"`: 18 failures;
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:91:  - FlexAttention builds its own Triton templates regardless of this setting. The model does not use it.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:92:  - Static-shape compiles and `bmm` numerics were not measured.
cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:93:  - The real-trunk backward was not element-compared above the bound.
