cookbook/decisions/kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only.md:104:- The real-trunk backward above the bound and the production compile path are verified. That is also the condition for retiring the guards.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:4:description: "Torch 2.9 Inductor max-autotune Triton GEMM templates wrap the 32-bit A-load offset once rows × GEMM input width exceeds 2^31 while the size argument stays int32 (measured at widths 4096, 768 and 512 and silent in the real trunk; output-wide GEMMs stayed correct to 2^32); this caused the reference PPO-from-BC crash. At `1ddc71d` the rebuilt trunk guard was measured correct at L−1 and rejected L; the packed path now chunks instead of rejecting (CPU-tested). Task 3.1 registers the model and dispatches the guarded trunk compile (CPU-tested). A measured A/B found ATEN-only (cuBLAS) GEMM backends correct above the bound, with no Triton GEMM template, at +4.5–6.5 % model-only update wall; compiled Kaggriculture regions now require that setting (CPU-tested), and the guards stay. Production compliance is unproven."
