cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:17:A controlled probe confirmed the threshold. It used a synthetic BF16 MLP (256→1024, GELU, 1024→256) with `torch.compile(mode="max-autotune-no-cudagraphs", dynamic=True)`, compiled at a small shape first. At M = 2,088,960 the compiled output matches eager within BF16 noise (max diff 0.0078). At M = 2,105,344 it faults. Environment: torch 2.9.0+cu128, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, driver 595.91.07. Hashes and logs are in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md`.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:22:- The bug is in compiler-generated code, so it is invisible in the model source. It can reappear for any compiled GEMM whose `rows × input width` exceeds 2³¹: rollouts, evaluation, BC, and other models with larger batches. In training, backward reads forward outputs as inputs, so the forward output width counts too (below).
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:38:- **Above the bound, nothing is reliable.** Whether a given M corrupts, faults or happens to be correct depends on the recompile hint and on autotune's backend choice. For example, cuBLAS won for a lone 512→256, and the trunk was correct again at 8.39M tokens after an i64 recompile. Recompilation is not a safety guarantee.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:43:- **Real-trunk backward.** It was not run at any size. The synthetic MLP backward faulted while compiling at L+1, which does not localize a backward-kernel threshold.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:48:- **Remedy in force: cuBLAS-only compiled GEMMs.** An A/B on the same pod changed one setting, `max_autotune_gemm_backends` from `"ATEN,TRITON,CPP"` to `"ATEN"` (branch `kg/rebuild-model` at `9bdd82d`, `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md` lines 259–303; Codex r2 APPROVE).
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:49:  - With the guard bypassed, every case that failed under the default backends was correct under ATEN-only. That covers the real packed trunk up to 8,387,470 tokens, Linear 768→256 and 512→256, and the synthetic MLP forward and backward (lines 269–272). The same run's default controls reproduced the corruption and the fault (line 274).
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:50:  - The ATEN caches hold no `triton_tem_` kernels, and autotune logs `num_triton_choices: 0` (lines 276–281).
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:52:  - Kaggriculture compiles now require the setting after a probed-stack check. Orbit is unchanged, and one process never compiles both games ([[kaggriculture-compiles-gemms-with-cublas-only|cuBLAS-only Decision]]). This is CPU-tested only.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:53:  - The A/B's limits carry over: FlexAttention, static shapes, `bmm`, the real-trunk backward above the bound and a single stack (lines 261 and 295–303). **The design bound and guards below therefore stay** as defence in depth until the real-trunk backward above the bound and the production compile path are verified.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:54:- **Design bound: keep every compiled region at M × max(in, out) < 2³¹ over its Linear layers (the strict rule the guard implements; whether equality is safe on the real trunk was never measured).** This follows from the measured input-side rule plus backward: dX = dY·W reads dY at the forward output width, and weight-gradient GEMMs reduce over M. It is not justified by an output-store overflow.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:64:- **Upgrades:** don't upgrade torch or drivers as a remedy without a separate measured decision. Rerun both probes and the ATEN-only A/B after any upgrade; the compile-stack check rejects an unprobed torch, triton or driver until then.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:68:- **Stack:** measured on torch 2.9.0+cu128, driver 595.91.07, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (sm_120). Triton 3.5.0 is the lockfile pin; its installed version was not captured.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:70:  - the real trunk's backward;
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:72:  - `bmm`, persistent-TMA and decompose-K paths (decompose-K is on by default and can apply to weight-gradient GEMMs);
